      "level": 2,
      "content": "Skeletal System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dmc5bxe",
      "content": "The adult human body contains 206 bones. The skeleton supports the body and protects vital organs."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Femur is the longest and strongest bone, while Stapes in the middle ear is the smallest bone in the human body.",
        "Mitochondria generate ATP and are frequently tested as the 'Powerhouse of the Cell'.",
        "Human Red Blood Cells (RBCs) lack a nucleus upon maturity to maximize oxygen transportation capacity."
      ],
      "id": "rfsf3nu"
    },
